## When Documentation Is Wrong

Documentation that claims a security property which isn't implemented is not a documentation bug. It's a **security defect**. False claims about encryption, authentication, access control, or data handling are unacceptable. They must be fixed immediately - either implement the feature or remove the claim. There is no third option.

